      [3] vec=(24,56,0)
      [0] str="<font color=\"#000000\" size=11>\r\n\r\nThese demonstration pages will take you through some of the most commonly used controls in XuiTool.\r\nTo run this demo, press the F5 key or click the 'File > Preview' menu option.\r\nDo this now...\r\n\r\n<br/>\r\n<font size=8>\r\n<br/>\r\n</font>\r\n\r\n<table>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"4%\"/>\r\n<td width=\"3%\" bgcolor=\"#808080\"/>\r\n<td width=\"86%\" bgcolor=\"#808080\">\r\n\r\n<font size=5>\r\n<br/>\r\n</font>\r\n\r\n<font color=\"#FFFFFF\" size=10>\r\nTo navigate through the controls/pages, you can use any of the following:\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The arrow keys on your keyboard, along with the A/B/X/Y keys</li>\r\n<li>The mouse cursor, and the left mouse button</li>\r\n<li>An Xbox 360 controller connected to your PC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n</font>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"3%\" bgcolor=\"#808080\"/>\r\n<td width=\"4%\"/>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<font size=8>\r\n<br/>\r\n</font>\r\n\r\nAll controls can be skinned using <i><b>Visuals</b></i> from a skin file.\r\nFor instance, this is how you would create two <i><b>Button</b></i> controls that look completely different from one another.\r\nIf the <i><b>Visual</b></i> property isn't specified for a control, it will use a <i><b>Visual</b></i> with the same name as the control's class (ie. <i>XuiButton</i>).\r\nTo see the <i><b>Visuals</b></i> being used in this demonstration, run the 'File > Open' menu option and select the <i>skin_default.xui</i> file.\r\n</font>\r\n\r\n"
